[{:db/id "q-32876/selection/75537d91227eed77c3ad3e995d8298bde54228244402622900c92b89b62655fd" :answer/id #uuid "3e3edef2-6cc6-5021-bee2-7a90f682335e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-i+\\frac{3}{2}\\,k+u(\\pi \\,j+\\,k)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32876/selection/84c120f944673544abb22b46f0a3eddb0979089e85074f26bfe43f9d02af257b" :answer/id #uuid "befbd5a4-c675-5da0-9912-b913adce33c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-i+\\frac{3}{2}\\,k+u(-\\pi \\,j-\\,k)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32876/selection/6f0c31e9fdc37312e91107bdee65f61e455d0373551042027bcefb75a8b24b99" :answer/id #uuid "6940bd89-4ab1-5c22-ac0d-fe0022283b39" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-i+\\frac{3}{2}\\,k+u(\\pi \\,i+\\,j)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32876/selection/b7b09475f1f30c72dab4c0c42b933b5acbcdfb5a3e07be8240c87b8e1258d40a" :answer/id #uuid "5e29cd53-1332-5338-9ca6-c391c313a8ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-i+\\frac{3}{2}\\,k+u(i+\\pi \\,j+\\,k)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32876/selection/10a099058ca09749d083f2614eff04aae533680cf7bf1b9594af2fbb5d5f745e" :answer/id #uuid "6f1ed178-5cf5-5d83-a3bc-dfd7c8a21552" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-i-\\frac{3}{2}\\,k+u(\\pi \\,i+\\,k)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32876/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9e75698a-e910-5bed-b0ad-fb527a02771e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-32876/selection/75537d91227eed77c3ad3e995d8298bde54228244402622900c92b89b62655fd" :answer-field/choices ["q-32876/selection/75537d91227eed77c3ad3e995d8298bde54228244402622900c92b89b62655fd" "q-32876/selection/84c120f944673544abb22b46f0a3eddb0979089e85074f26bfe43f9d02af257b" "q-32876/selection/6f0c31e9fdc37312e91107bdee65f61e455d0373551042027bcefb75a8b24b99" "q-32876/selection/b7b09475f1f30c72dab4c0c42b933b5acbcdfb5a3e07be8240c87b8e1258d40a" "q-32876/selection/10a099058ca09749d083f2614eff04aae533680cf7bf1b9594af2fbb5d5f745e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-32876" :question/id #uuid "33bfb8ae-51e5-575a-aee2-202f3434e957" :question/math-academy-id "q-32876" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the equation of the tangent to the curve $r(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t\\,j+t\\,k$ at the point $P(-1,0,\\frac{3}{2}),$ valid for real values of $u?$" :question/worked-solution "The point $P(-1,0,\\frac{3}{2})$ is at the tip of $r(t)$ for some specific value ${t}_{0}$ of the parameter $t.$ At this point,  the vector ${r}^{′}({t}_{0})$ is tangent to the curve, so the tangent line to the curve at $P$ can be parametrized as\n\n$$\nR(u)=r({t}_{0})+u\\,{r}^{′}({t}_{0}),\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to $P.$ We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =-i+0\\,j+\\frac{3}{2}\\,k \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t\\,j+t\\,k & =-i+0\\,j+\\frac{3}{2}\\,k,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand equating the coefficients of $i,j,$ and $k$ yields the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t=-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t=0 \\\\ t=\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get $t=\\frac{3}{2}.$ This value also satisfies the other two equations. Therefore, $P(-1,0,\\frac{3}{2})$ is at the tip of the vector $r(\\frac{3}{2}).$  \n\nWe calculate ${r}^{′}(t):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,k \\\\  & =\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t\\,i-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t\\,j+\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we evaluate ${r}^{′}(t)$ at $t=\\frac{3}{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(\\frac{3}{2}) & =\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})\\,i-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})\\,j+\\,k \\\\  & =0\\,i+\\pi \\,j+\\,k \\\\  & =\\pi \\,j+\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the given curve at the point $P(-1,0,\\frac{3}{2})$ is\n\n$$\nR(u)=-i+\\frac{3}{2}\\,k+u\\,(\\pi \\,j+\\,k),\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-32876/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "60e28b26-0eb7-51ed-bcf9-2660b98a6028"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-32876"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-75524/selection/ff992f3bfbf9256bb8a93ba4418b1d3fc4bf7775122685039de83403d09a1dca" :answer/id #uuid "4447b138-bebf-5afe-b78d-5672fa327263" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75524/selection/89af89b3efd3f5ca5dab5b81197aeb518571be47628f794fda750dff1672fbc8" :answer/id #uuid "872d74c2-4fff-5731-82a9-452b9fc6e3ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},-\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75524/selection/0a0871df80bcfb7bae60610dff34b0350d54dd28dacbef652911d23b9937aec6" :answer/id #uuid "b2ee5cbf-c033-5a7a-8ae9-67d407a5777f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,3)$ and $(1,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75524/selection/20ddf98f39441025e2785a20fbf29739ec32eedfa5b1e5eb9bd892192e9349e9" :answer/id #uuid "090528e6-30ba-5d9b-859c-cbc8f3855140" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,0)$ and $(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},-\\frac{3}{2})$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75524/selection/9e826a56ad51f1ba420550a47ccaffc6d0278c148ffdbc533536c2f23982847b" :answer/id #uuid "8f2afec9-7f6c-5645-af5d-df036d1b6c87" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,3)$ and $(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},-\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2})$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-75524/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a25f1b88-efd6-5bc5-adff-d60834a59ef9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-75524/selection/0a0871df80bcfb7bae60610dff34b0350d54dd28dacbef652911d23b9937aec6" :answer-field/choices ["q-75524/selection/ff992f3bfbf9256bb8a93ba4418b1d3fc4bf7775122685039de83403d09a1dca" "q-75524/selection/89af89b3efd3f5ca5dab5b81197aeb518571be47628f794fda750dff1672fbc8" "q-75524/selection/0a0871df80bcfb7bae60610dff34b0350d54dd28dacbef652911d23b9937aec6" "q-75524/selection/20ddf98f39441025e2785a20fbf29739ec32eedfa5b1e5eb9bd892192e9349e9" "q-75524/selection/9e826a56ad51f1ba420550a47ccaffc6d0278c148ffdbc533536c2f23982847b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-75524" :question/id #uuid "f1e2ae0c-272c-5ed9-a620-4462d5cc1c06" :question/math-academy-id "q-75524" :question/problem "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,,\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩,t\\in [0,\\pi )$ find all of the points at which ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $r(t)$ are perpendicular." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the derivative of $r(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,,\\,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors  $r(t)$ and ${r}^{′}(t)$ are perpendicular for some value of the parameter $t$ if and only if $r(t)\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)=0.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t)\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =0 \\\\ ⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,,\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\cdot ⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,,\\,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot (-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) & =0 \\\\ -8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡2t & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $t\\in [0,\\pi )$, the only solutions are $t=0$ and $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\nFinally, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0) & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡0\\,,\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡0⟩=⟨0\\,,\\,3⟩, \\\\ r(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,,\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2}⟩=⟨1\\,,\\,0⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n we conclude that $r(t)$ and ${r}^{′}(t)$ are perpendicular at the points $(0,3)$ and $(1,0).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-75524/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "297a4812-a87a-592a-818a-8c8d3d3f7868"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-75524"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-126837/selection/cdecce4833587304131c3dfda8357f59de44c5a3f3c003fa610cefcd45470b8a" :answer/id #uuid "e9630d09-3e39-5ca5-a0cd-e5ccf0c0b813" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨27,7⟩+u⟨9,7⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126837/selection/ceed29f2440a8f7fd2d87ebf236ae220802de86f67e4fc54473a87fd4b1efc12" :answer/id #uuid "026a915b-4342-55ee-ac65-fa0cfbb756c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨9,1⟩+u⟨9,7⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126837/selection/87c9fc26290b3d8c5bdda4b4b03c2c9abe2267c5e08cd1e4d58dbcf3042d11d2" :answer/id #uuid "cfbc2e52-a663-5cb7-98b4-0305e5f6711f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨9,1⟩+u⟨27,6⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126837/selection/d1022cbda85efd7b0268999509b220d7ee7c7d8751e666ed4053f0c9205dded6" :answer/id #uuid "3c18be1c-75ea-5a56-96c5-929ff8dd2e86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨27,7⟩+u⟨14,6⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126837/selection/e4d5b088bdf45c85f8b8c0ecd68f13ed812c7a5ef6489fe2314f8cb424262fb1" :answer/id #uuid "2c422e92-660c-5616-b868-8ebcf95bf214" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨27,7⟩+u⟨27,6⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-126837/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "727d0217-ff47-55c7-97e2-76ebbeb27bcf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-126837/selection/e4d5b088bdf45c85f8b8c0ecd68f13ed812c7a5ef6489fe2314f8cb424262fb1" :answer-field/choices ["q-126837/selection/cdecce4833587304131c3dfda8357f59de44c5a3f3c003fa610cefcd45470b8a" "q-126837/selection/ceed29f2440a8f7fd2d87ebf236ae220802de86f67e4fc54473a87fd4b1efc12" "q-126837/selection/87c9fc26290b3d8c5bdda4b4b03c2c9abe2267c5e08cd1e4d58dbcf3042d11d2" "q-126837/selection/d1022cbda85efd7b0268999509b220d7ee7c7d8751e666ed4053f0c9205dded6" "q-126837/selection/e4d5b088bdf45c85f8b8c0ecd68f13ed812c7a5ef6489fe2314f8cb424262fb1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-126837" :question/id #uuid "ff8b7d1f-787a-5846-b2f9-a68bcb9d4f3d" :question/math-academy-id "q-126837" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the equation of the tangent to the curve $r(t)=⟨{t}^{3},{t}^{2}-2⟩$ at the point where $t=3,$  valid for all  real values of $u?$" :question/worked-solution "At the point where $t=3,$ the vector ${r}^{′}(3)$ is tangent to the curve, so the tangent line to the curve at $P$ can be parametrized as\n \n\n$$\nR(u)=r(3)+u{r}^{′}(3),\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we find $r(3):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(3) & =⟨{3}^{3},{3}^{2}-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨27,7⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{t}^{2},2t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we evaluate ${r}^{′}(t)$ at $t=3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(3) & =⟨3(3)^{2},2(3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨27,6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the given curve at the point where $t=3$ is\n\n$$\nR(u)=⟨27,7⟩+u⟨27,6⟩,\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-126837/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "60e28b26-0eb7-51ed-bcf9-2660b98a6028"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-126837"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
